cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software

title: "Ktupad Core: A Lightweight PHP PDO Engine for JSON-Driven CRUD Operations"
abstract: >
  Ktupad Core is a single-entry-point MVC micro-framework built on PHP PDO,
  designed for rapid backend API development with minimal dependencies.
  All CRUD operations are dispatched via JSON payloads, enabling decoupled
  frontend architectures suitable for low-resource server environments and
  educational institutional systems. The framework implements Front Controller,
  Active Record, and Command patterns through a flat three-layer inheritance
  chain (koneksi → ktupad → mod), with built-in role-based access control,
  token authentication, file upload handling, and CSV import functionality.
  Originally developed in 2019 and registered as intellectual property
  EC00201952487 at the Direktorat Jenderal Kekayaan Intelektual (DJKI),
  Republic of Indonesia, Ktupad Core serves as the foundational architecture
  preceding BayamJS (2023) and DonatJS (2024) in the Ktupad ecosystem.

